Crypto lifecycle coverage
=========================

lifecycle_test includes the production daemon and calls its teardown helper
with real PD_DAEMON children. It checks child reaping, closed process handles,
release of inherited pipe writers, repeated empty cleanup and failure reporting.
reaper_cleanup calls the actual start_reaper function and tears down its returned
process descriptor. No crypto control device or installed-bundle authority is
supplied in that case; it does not test key reclamation decisions.

provider_test covers the real channel provider and crypto descriptor operations
in the native guest. policy_test covers the provider's key/digest/random policy.

Remaining integration gates: installed bundle startup and diagnostic exit codes,
protected worker termination, SwitchBoard idle decline and explicit stop/restart,
cleanup before acknowledgement, and reclamation while real install roots change.
Abrupt parent death is separate from controlled teardown. Delivered descriptors
are not revoked by stopping their worker. Device and Crypto now delegate teardown to libservice service_processes_stop;
these tests therefore exercise the shared implementation. Procdesc ownership
is exclusive and tracking nodes are consumed even on error. Other providers
require separate review of their worker ownership and shutdown contracts.
